        "merged_at": null
      },
      "body": "`health.py --json` treats URL-encoded Markdown links as literal filenames. For example, an index entry pointing to `concepts/Caf%C3%A9%20Guide.md` reports both a stale entry and an unindexed page even when `concepts/Café Guide.md` exists.\n\nI decode link targets once before comparing them with files on disk. The regression runs the actual health CLI in a temporary wiki, covering UTF-8/spaces, a literal `%20` filename, unchanged `+` and plain links, and genuine missing/unindexed pages.\n\nValidation on Windows 11:\n- `python -m unittest discover -s tests -v`: the CLI regression passes on Python 3.10.20, 3.11.15, 3.12.13 and 3.13.12; it fails on baseline `839f5ac2d375ed44769ea1b2c6acfbe02e5580ac`.\n- `python tools/health.py --json`: the same five-page fixture goes from three stale entries and three unindexed pages to only the intentionally deleted page and orphan page. The repository's existing wiki also remains healthy.\n- `python -m compileall -q tools tests` and `git diff --check` pass.\n\nVerified candidate: `594ba14fde21a0b590a6633d2d2892a68bf41d38`. The CLI validation uses local files and makes no LLM calls.\r\n",
      "closed_by": null,
