      "body": "## Summary\n\n`python tools/pdf2md.py --help` raises `UnicodeEncodeError` when stdout uses cp1252 because the help epilog contains Unicode arrows.\n\nUse ASCII punctuation in the help epilog so both `--help` and `-h` work with cp1252, ASCII, and UTF-8 output streams without changing the user's stream encoding.\n\nCloses #79.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Added a subprocess regression test covering both help flags with all three encodings. The cp1252 and ASCII cases fail on the original code; all six cases now pass.\n- `python -m unittest discover -s tests -v` passes on Python 3.12.\n- Subprocesses use `-S`, so no third-party conversion dependencies, network requests, or model calls are needed.\n\nThe encoding regression is simulated with `PYTHONIOENCODING`; a native Windows run was not available.\n",
      "closed_by": null,
