      "body": "## Description\nWhen ingestion converts a non-Markdown source to Markdown, the conversion function derives an output path with the same stem and writes it without checking whether that sibling already exists. For example, if raw/paper.pdf and a hand-written raw/paper.md are both present, conversion can replace the existing Markdown content.\n\n## Expected behavior\nExisting content should be preserved by default with a clear collision message, or replacement should require an explicit opt-in consistent with the other conversion path.\n\n## Evidence\nThis behavior is in the ingestion conversion path. The guard in the batch conversion path covers a different entry point and does not protect this path. Isolated checks confirmed the output target and source behavior; no file was overwritten.\n\nThis report concerns data preservation during ordinary conversion and does not claim that any file was actually lost.",
      "closed_by": null,
